        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: দৈবাৎ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দৈবাৎ — doibāt — \"by chance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বাজারে দৈবাৎ আমার পুরনো বন্ধুর সঙ্গে দেখা হল। Bājāre doibāt āmār purôno bôndhur sôngge dækhā hôlô. By chance I met my old friend at the market."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দৈবাৎ (doibāt) is the Sanskrit form daivāt, \"from fate\", of daiva, \"coming from the gods, fate\" (Monier-Williams): by the gods' doing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
