              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কাকতালীয় (kāktālīyô) is Sanskrit kākatālīya (Monier-Williams), from a fable: a crow lands on a palm tree at the very moment a fruit falls, and the two events only look connected."
            }
          ]
        },
